/* book exam traps: Forgetting the 1/(2π) factor in the inverse transform. The forward transform has no such factor in this convention. | Mixing f in Hz with ω in rad/s. Use X(ω)=∫x(t)e−jωtdt and remember ω=2πf. | Using the wrong denominator for e−atu(t). It is 1/(a+jω), not 1/(a−jω), and the lower limit is 0 because of u(t). | Assuming a time-limited pulse is band-limited. A rectangular pulse has sinc tails that never end, so its spectrum is nonzero at arbitrarily high ω. | Treating δ(ω−ω₀) as a finite value. It is a density with unit area; the spectrum of a sinusoid is an impulse, not a tall finite spike. */
